# API architecture

## Do

- Wire HTTP in routes and delegate to controllers; map requests in controllers and call services only.
- Keep business logic in services to be controlled from one place; read and write `data/` only through `file-storage.service.js`.
- Add route, controller, service, validator, and tests for new endpoints.

## Do not

- Put business logic or file I/O in routes or controllers.
- Import services circularly across layers.
- Bypass validators for user-controlled retrospective data.
